col	cirislens.federation_attestations	16	subject_key_ids	jsonb	true	'[]'::jsonb				v3.7.0 (CIRISPersist#146, CEG 0.6 §4.2). OPTIONAL list of consent-holder key_ids for this attestation. Each entry MAY be a federation_keys.key_id OR a canonical-hash identifier (CEG 0.6 §4.2.2). Default [] = status quo (producer-only authority). Substrate does NOT FK-enforce that entries are federation_keys rows — canonical-hash subjects (Discord user-ids, external party identifiers) are valid per CEG 0.6 design.	
col	cirislens.federation_attestations	17	withdraws_admission_rule	smallint	false					v3.7.0 (CIRISPersist#146, CEG 0.6 §3.2.3). Per-rule audit metadata: which of the 4 admission rules admitted this withdraws. 1 = producer self-revocation (legacy), 2 = subject self-revocation (CEG 0.6 NEW), 3 = delegates_to proxy with consent_revocation scope (CEG 0.6 NEW), 4 = delegates_to chain via any of 1-3. NULL on non-withdraws rows. Populated at admission time in v3.8.0+ once the 4-rule admission gate lands.	
col	cirislens.federation_attestations	18	cohort_scope	text	true	'federation'::text				v3.9.0 (CIRISPersist#150, CEG §4.2.4). Closed-set producer-side visibility scope. Default 'federation' (pre-v3.9.0 backward-compat). Orthogonal to subject_key_ids[] (revocability authority). §8.1.8 feed compositions filter by this column.	
col	cirislens.federation_attestations	19	tier	text	true	'federation'::text				v4.4 (CIRISPersist#171, CEG §10.1.3/§10.1.5) — local (producer-only authority, signature deferred, visible only to the producing occurrence) | federation (hybrid-signed, federation-visible). DEFAULT federation. CHECK federation_attestations_federation_tier_signed enforces federation ⟹ non-empty classical signature (AV-60).	
