rel	cirislens.feedback_mappings	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	v1.5.18 (CIRISPersist#59 #10) — feedback_mappings substrate. Absorbs CIRISAgent ciris_engine.db.feedback_mappings; the link between an inbound feedback Discord-message (or analogous wire-message id) and the agent thought it resolved against. 5 columns matching the agent. target_thought_id FK to cirislens.thoughts(thought_id), DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED, only fires for non-NULL values (PG handles null FKs natively). Designed as a dedicated substrate rather than folded into cirisgraph_edges — feedback rides on typed-substrate FKs (thoughts), not graph-node FKs.
rel	cirislens.freshness_floor	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	
rel	cirislens.goals	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	v60.0.0 (CIRISPersist#988 item 4) — the projection of the goal:{scale}:v1 rows this node holds: one row per declaration (goal_id = its attestation_id), the head of its amendment chain (attestation_id), retired at the winning withdraws, absent once recanted. Written only by the attestation plane executor; byte-equal to its from-rows rebuild. A row with NULL attestation_id is a pre-V204 typed goal awaiting the rehome.
rel	cirislens.hard_case_events	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	
rel	cirislens.identity_canonical_binding	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	v3.9.0 (CIRISPersist#146 Ask 6, CEG §3.2.3 rule 3 + §4.2.2). Index of canonical-hash subjects bound to federation-enrolled identities. Populated when an identity:canonical_binding attestation is admitted. Consulted at withdraws admission to admit rule-3 proxy-chain revocations.
rel	cirislens.identity_sequences	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	v1.7.1 (CIRISPersist#83) — atomic monotonic sequence counters keyed (identity, stream). next_value is the LAST issued value; the issuing UPSERT bumps then RETURNs.
rel	cirislens.incident_records	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	v0.8.3 (CIRISPersist#37) — incident records absorbed from CIRISAgent IncidentManagementService. Correlation-keyed dedup on record (bumps occurrences for matching open incident); open→investigating→resolved→closed state machine enforced server-side (AV-55).
rel	cirislens.key_escrows	r	p		{ciris=arwdDxt/ciris,cirislens_reader=r/ciris}	CC 4.4.3.2.8 archive_custody working index (CIRISPersist#752): custody metadata, never key material, never a claims plane.
